WEBVTT

NOTE Generated by scripts/captions-guide.py - do not edit by hand.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.149
Insights opens the console on today.

2
00:00:02.149 --> 00:00:05.193
It tells you who is next
through the door and when,

3
00:00:05.193 --> 00:00:09.610
how many appointments you are holding,
what they are expected to bring in,

4
00:00:09.610 --> 00:00:11.443
and how full the day is.

5
00:00:13.900 --> 00:00:18.287
The menu reaches the rest of the
console — your services and your staff,

6
00:00:18.287 --> 00:00:23.806
the client book, product orders, offers and
loyalty, payroll and tax, and your plan.

7
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:28.324
The calendar's day view lists every
appointment with its customer,

8
00:00:28.324 --> 00:00:33.323
service and stylist — and on each one, the
buttons to complete it, mark a no-show,

9
00:00:33.323 --> 00:00:34.333
or cancel.

10
00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:39.149
The week view counts the
bookings on each day,

11
00:00:39.149 --> 00:00:42.562
so you can see where the work
is landing before it arrives.

12
00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:46.763
The list view drops the grid and
shows the same bookings as upcoming,

13
00:00:46.763 --> 00:00:48.437
completed and cancelled.

14
00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.691
Opening a booking gives you
the services and the total,

15
00:00:51.691 --> 00:00:53.112
the loyalty points it earns,

16
00:00:53.112 --> 00:00:56.862
and somewhere to record the payment
once it is taken at the salon.

17
00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:02.179
The queue board shows how many people
are waiting, roughly how long that is,

18
00:01:02.179 --> 00:01:04.380
and which of your barbers are free.

19
00:01:04.380 --> 00:01:06.730
Call next moves the line along.

20
00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:13.177
Show QR gives you a code customers
scan to put themselves in the line.

21
00:01:13.177 --> 00:01:17.839
Print it for the counter, or copy the
link and send it to your staff group.

22
00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:21.684
And when somebody simply walks
in, you can add them yourself —

23
00:01:21.684 --> 00:01:26.177
their name and number if you want them,
the services, a stylist and a time.

24
00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:30.209
Your services carry a price, a
length, and who they are for.

25
00:01:30.209 --> 00:01:34.010
The switch on each one takes it
off the menu without deleting it,

26
00:01:34.010 --> 00:01:37.802
and you can start from a common
service or write your own.

27
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:42.078
Products work the same way.

28
00:01:42.078 --> 00:01:47.152
Anything out of stock shows as sold
out, and customers cannot order it.

29
00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:50.586
Staff lists everyone
customers can book with.

30
00:01:51.100 --> 00:01:54.658
Each one has their own record —
whether they are active and bookable,

31
00:01:54.658 --> 00:01:58.371
whether their account is linked so
they can sign in, what they are paid,

32
00:01:58.371 --> 00:02:00.421
and which services they perform.

33
00:02:00.900 --> 00:02:03.841
Packs bundle visits a
customer buys in advance.

34
00:02:03.841 --> 00:02:09.372
They are paid for at the salon, so you
confirm each one once the money is in hand.

35
00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:14.323
The client book counts your regulars,
who has lapsed, and who is booked in —

36
00:02:14.323 --> 00:02:18.157
and sorts them by their spend,
their visits, or their name.

37
00:02:20.700 --> 00:02:24.185
Opening a client shows how often
they come and what they have spent,

38
00:02:24.185 --> 00:02:28.121
a private note only you can see,
and every appointment they have had.

39
00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.835
Product orders arrive as new, move to
ready when they are waiting at the counter,

40
00:02:32.835 --> 00:02:34.176
and close as done.

41
00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:37.968
And messages from customers
all land in one place.

42
00:02:38.500 --> 00:02:42.753
An offer is a promotion you run
yourself — twenty percent off colour,

43
00:02:42.753 --> 00:02:44.110
or a festival special.

44
00:02:44.110 --> 00:02:48.085
It shows on your salon page
and in the customer home feed.

45
00:02:50.600 --> 00:02:55.069
The loyalty programme earns customers points
on every visit, or on what they spend,

46
00:02:55.069 --> 00:02:57.784
and you decide what
those points are worth.

47
00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:02.427
When somebody cashes a reward in,
you confirm it here with their code.

48
00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:07.288
Payroll adds each stylist's base pay to a
commission on the bookings they actually

49
00:03:07.288 --> 00:03:09.079
completed, month by month.

50
00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.236
And the tax report estimates your position
for the year on a presumptive basis,

51
00:03:14.236 --> 00:03:15.761
with your filing deadline.

52
00:03:15.761 --> 00:03:20.034
It is an estimate — confirm it
with an accountant before you file.

53
00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:24.572
Settings is where your salon
describes itself — its name and type,

54
00:03:24.572 --> 00:03:28.768
its address and its pin on the map,
its phone number and its photos.

55
00:03:28.768 --> 00:03:30.834
This is what customers see.

56
00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:34.931
Tho comes in three plans.

57
00:03:34.931 --> 00:03:40.747
Basic gets you listed and taking bookings,
with today's numbers and a day calendar.

58
00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:44.486
Anything beyond that says so
plainly rather than hiding.

59
00:03:44.486 --> 00:03:48.407
The walk-in line you saw earlier
is part of the Growth plan.

60
00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:52.886
Every locked feature names the plan it
belongs to and what that plan costs,

61
00:03:52.886 --> 00:03:54.933
so nothing is a surprise later.

62
00:03:55.400 --> 00:03:56.955
Basic gets you listed.

63
00:03:56.955 --> 00:04:02.114
Growth adds unlimited stylists, the
week view, reminders, full analytics,

64
00:04:02.114 --> 00:04:06.566
the client book, the storefront,
loyalty and the walk-in queue.

65
00:04:06.566 --> 00:04:10.782
And Pro adds commissions and
payroll for busier teams.
